1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:01,759
What if the Sun vanished?

2
00:00:02,009 --> 00:00:04,526
For about eight minutes and twenty seconds,

3
00:00:04,586 --> 00:00:06,037
you'd notice nothing.

4
00:00:06,217 --> 00:00:08,073
Sunlight already in space

5
00:00:08,103 --> 00:00:10,236
would still be racing toward Earth.

6
00:00:10,436 --> 00:00:12,164
Then daylight would end.

7
00:00:12,464 --> 00:00:14,832
In this impossible thought experiment,

8
00:00:14,882 --> 00:00:18,466
changes in gravity also travel at light speed.

9
00:00:18,616 --> 00:00:20,579
Earth would leave its solar orbit,

10
00:00:20,629 --> 00:00:22,805
moving roughly along a tangent.

11
00:00:23,005 --> 00:00:25,031
But we wouldn't instantly freeze.

12
00:00:25,131 --> 00:00:27,499
The oceans and atmosphere store heat.

13
00:00:27,659 --> 00:00:30,731
Without sunlight, photosynthesis would stop,

14
00:00:30,811 --> 00:00:32,753
and the surface would keep cooling.

15
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,313
Now the twist.

16
00:00:34,553 --> 00:00:35,299
Life

17
00:00:35,334 --> 00:00:36,017
could

18
00:00:36,052 --> 00:00:37,055
survive.

19
00:00:37,235 --> 00:00:39,965
Around seafloor vents, some microbes

20
00:00:40,005 --> 00:00:43,035
use chemical energy instead of sunlight.

21
00:00:43,185 --> 00:00:45,083
Earth's internal heat wouldn't disappear

22
00:00:45,103 --> 00:00:46,234
with the Sun.

23
00:00:46,434 --> 00:00:48,525
Our world could lose its star,

24
00:00:48,685 --> 00:00:51,735
without immediately losing every living thing.
